s\n*","skill_name":"managing-data-asset-access"},{"rank_order":4,"title":"managing-amazon-kinesis-data-streams","skill_description":"Operates data delivery and queues in Amazon Kinesis Data Streams (KDS). Covers delivering a stream to Iceberg tables on S3 Tables or to S3 buckets, and queue-based consumption: receive, acknowledge, visibility timeout, and migrating KCL, GetRecords, or Lambda consumers. Applies when records can be processed independently, without shard ordering: to consume a stream without managing shards, leases, or checkpoints, run more consumers than shards, or stop one bad record blocking a shard, whether or not they mention Kinesis queues.\nTriggers: Kinesis Data Streams, KDS, streaming tables, stream to S3, stream to Iceberg, stream to S3 Tables, KDS delivery, KDS channel, CreateChannel, data channel, data freshness, dead-letter queue, KDS lakehouse, serverless Kinesis delivery, Firehose alternative for KDS, zero-ops Kinesis to S3, ReceiveQueueRecords, Kinesis dead-letter records. Not for Kinesis Data Firehose, Kinesis Video Streams, Managed Service for Apache Flink, SQS dead-letter queues, or tuning a KCL app.\n\n\nServices: kinesis, s3, s3tables, glue\nTasks: troubleshoot, debug, optimize, deploy, monitor\nPersona: developer, devops, architect\nWorkload: streaming, data-analytics","skill_name":"managing-amazon-kinesis-data-streams"}]}}"}]}], "label": "Check Bedrock token burndown for Claude Sonnet 5", "parent_id": "763143d1-540e-4ff9-a4fd-14b89d763641"}

